# Key Insights

## 1. Most In-Demand Skills

Python and SQL appear among the most frequently requested skills in data-related job postings.

This suggests that programming and database skills are important for many data roles.

## 2. Skill Combinations

Several analytics-related jobs mention combinations of tools such as SQL, Python, Power BI, Excel, and cloud platforms.

This shows that employers often expect a mix of programming, data handling, and visualization skills.

## 3. Salary Patterns

Salary levels vary depending on job title, role type, and location.

Senior and specialized technical roles generally show higher salary values compared with entry-level or general analyst roles.

## 4. Location Trends

Some countries and regions show stronger demand for data-related roles.

This may reflect the concentration of technology companies, business hubs, and analytics-driven industries.

## 5. Dashboard Usefulness

The dashboard allows users to quickly explore job-market trends by filtering job title and country.

This makes it useful for understanding which skills and roles are common in the data job market.
